The allegation read as follows:-
(i) the marriage of opposite party no. 2 was solemnized at Patna with Dr. Vivek Ranjan on 27.04.2015 who is a resident of Begusarai for which her mother had given Rs. 5 lakhs worth 'stridhan' and further Rs. 7 lakhs were given for the household materials;
(ii) allegation is that after the marriage, the father-in- law proposed that he along with O.P. no.2 will open a pathological lab in Begusarai which was consented by all the other accused persons;
(iii) further, the husband told her to take loan for buying flat at Patna which was also repeated by her father-in- law and mother-in-law.

